# ORIGINAL: TB2's mutant list — no swipl-devel counterpart.
# tools/mutants/TB2.py — the mutation battery of TAB1 TB2 (tabling worklists, SCCs, completion and the engine hooks): src/pl-tabling.jl (the
# components, the worklist sets, the clusters and the suspension index, the worklist, `$tbl_pop_worklist/2`, `$tbl_wkl_*`, `$tbl_wkl_work/6`,
# `$tbl_table_complete_all/3`, `$tbl_leader_complete/4`, `tbl_leader_finished`, `tbl_create_subcomponent`, `tbl_reset_add_answer`, the inspection
# predicates), src/pl-wam.jl (the `dtbl_reset6` branches of `I_RESET` and `I_EXITRESET`, `I_CALLCLEANUP`, `callCleanupHandler`) and src/pl-cont.jl
# (`push_continuation_list`). Run ONCE, in CI (.github/workflows/mutation.yml; locally: tools/mutate.sh run). Format: tools/mutate_drive.py's (as TB0.py, PIN1.py):
# `id`, `file`, `old` (must occur EXACTLY ONCE), `new`, optional `equivalent` and `targets`. NOT RUN: written edit-only on wip/tb2 (2026-11-10, nothing compiled);
# every KILL below is read off the rows of test/core_lang/test_tabling_worklist_swipl.jl (TW: 16 rows twl01-08 = left recursion tw_path/2, twm01-08 = mutual
# recursion tw_ev/tw_od and tw_r1/tw_r2, then the white-box `ld.tabling.component === nothing` at the end of its first testset), so the first hand-run
# replaces this header with the true verdicts. A KILL names the row whose pinned answer must differ; "or a hang": the battery's time limit decides a mutant
# that loops (tools/mutate_drive.py `expect`), and the kernel answer of every row is itself UNVERIFIED until the stack gate.
# THE ROWS READ: twl01 every pair, twl02 the nodes from a, twl03/04 yes/no, twl05 the count 12, twl06/07 the table status `complete` after completion, twl08 a
# second call gives the same answers; twm01/02 the two tables of one SCC, twm03 a call in the middle of the SCC, twm04 and twm08 the table status of both tables
# of an SCC, twm05/06 the closure through a second predicate, twm07 a bound first argument (a fresh variant inside nothing).
# The upstream flow the rows run (vendor/swipl-devel/boot/tabling.pl, the pin): `run_leader/6` :640-669 (activate, `'$tbl_pop_worklist'`, `completion_step`, `'$tbl_leader_complete'`,
# `'$tbl_wkl_make_follower'` for status `merged` :662), `completion/3` :866-880, `completion_/1` :883-891 and `'$tbl_wkl_work'/6` (:893-940).
# DEFERRED KILL (audit D-0374 item 2, as PIN1.py): a row declared `equivalent="DEFERRED KILL: owner ..."` has no killing assertion yet — no row of TW reads what the mutant
# changes; it must SURVIVE the battery, and the owner step's new row replaces the declaration. Owners: TB3 = answers, subsumptive tables (the suspension index
# with an instance: `$tbl_wkl_add_suspension/3`, the keyed `sindex_*` candidates) and the white-box counters; TB4 = WFS (tnot: `negative`, `neg_delayed`,
# `needs_answer_gc`, `$tbl_pop_worklist`'s negative branch, the component status of a finished SCC); TB5 = abolish, exceptions out of a tabled goal, the inspection
# predicates (`$tbl_scc/1`, `$tbl_scc_data/2`, `$tbl_worklist_data/2`) and `$tbl_wkl_done/1` (no caller in boot/tabling.pl at the pin); TB6 = IDG (the refusals).
